xt :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71876/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "8e897539-7b0f-5059-85f1-c18f0166caa0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71876/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "bf463b44-c338-5d2b-89e0-a6a466d2f78e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71876/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "5b0196c7-8e6e-5b19-b105-23b10d835fb7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71876/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e101af72-681a-5404-804d-9c959a6f14f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71876/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-71876/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-71876/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-71876/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-71876/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-71876/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71876" :question/id #uuid "b9625dd0-98eb-5747-8995-333316814407" :question/math-academy-id "q-71876" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $CD=DC={I}_{3}$\n- $CE=EC={I}_{3}$\n- $D={C}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $CD=DC={I}_{3}.$ Computing $CD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $DC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DC & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true. As a result, $D={C}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $CE=EC={I}_{3}.$ Computing $CE$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CE & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71876/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71876"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186261704 :question/answer-fields 17592186275019] {:db/id "q-78257/selection/ma-v1/a4c654bfa33b1be7f2d9aa999232b0e887e4386897ee6d910d7a95e48c325ae6/b4109f6a20f5aacc3a225a65a4ea9995114f02ef143899a0c038fc5896b7a552" :answer/id #uuid "10ee06aa-4179-587e-a705-928a9db9a24e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7825