704692aa057a6c68" "q-120789/selection/c73ea123c6d9fe8bdc48494d7559918f87841f24d6dc002c4a5f4c974229732b" "q-120789/selection/13fd502baba56158e4e61f5eb40f4b059510d3395aada301eacf5e01467bfe5d" "q-120789/selection/d7f4e37414472759751e5982719c2f624619b679ba2f26ce562e46be3bc604b1" "q-120789/selection/a44e9149dfc801645c466c1538922ed7ded42c28c991f0c637d1dc8c37cedf0c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120789" :question/id #uuid "4653a01e-6fa4-5345-8443-e064ea5e4a3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-120789" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035241/assets/8197d1111bbd4c3b8908bc12cbc58561ffd23fe06d9f9fa99f9ab815ed78733f.png)\n\nThe graph shows a portion of the curve $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and $y=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Which of the following generates the $x$-values of all of their points of intersection? Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "At the intersection points, the $y$-values are the same for both graphs. This gives the equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{2}.$ \n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $2$nd quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Since $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x<0,$ the second solution must lie in the third quadrant, and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035241/assets/ba34bf96662682ec433c3ade0bf3f118638212101a0729fe95bbae05aee8bf1e.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$  lies in the $3$rd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the general solution for the given equation is \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi ,\\,x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+2n\\pi .\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-120789/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff04ceeb-c9f6-5562-b494-204eb62d7f5b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120789"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186260204 :question/answer-fields 17592186274668] {:db/id "q-36743/selection/ma-v1/499676dfd0e10b3c1290b1dc468aca05eb808474f1fc2a2d712f2855dec6fff4/5e940f3cd00db401dff550023f9d7846ee8e88d0ab438012f7900921005438a1" :answer/id #uuid "98096e47-a475-5b71-bad4-5ae551f13075" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b=-1,\\,c=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36743/selection/ma-v1/499676dfd0e10b3c1290b1dc468aca05eb808474f1fc2a2d712f2855dec6fff4/f27ff288677794caac4d4dfa7f98017b6b8ccdddb43e5f1b2933181b33799f02" :answer/id #uuid "ebf6b84d-3f14-5e02-857b-fd98aa91ed39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b=-1,\\,c=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36743/selection/ma-v1/499676dfd0e10b3c1290b1dc468aca05eb808474f1fc2a2d712f2855dec6fff4/f9c789b092ee45fec89a4c6533fa375159bd93dcd3e732fe020b0e6879291539" :answer/id #uuid "bc19e557-4429-5048-91cb-d3f69a5ff392" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b=1,\\,c=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36743/selection/ma-v1/499676dfd0e10b3c1290b1dc468aca05eb808474f1fc2a2d712f2855dec6fff4/4dd529595d8741a6abef273107fff951ac48930bf03b48480053febd524d662c" :answer/id #uuid "11976953-3174-5a9b-8f1b-4169d90dd819" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b=1,\\,c=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36743/selection/ma-v1/499676dfd0e10b3c1290b1dc468aca05eb808474f1fc2a2d712f2855dec6fff4/02624510b3cc4035b51fda35d270d33f4e22b550c4247cd3fefe4ce345b57264" :answer/id #uuid "a948c07f-0c7c-55e3-878d-2023a4de22fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b=1,\\,c=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-36743/selection/ma-v1/499676dfd0e10b3c1290b1dc468aca05eb808474f1fc2a2d71