U$ that is not in the set $B.$\n\nThe elements of $U$ that are not in $B$ are $4,$ $8,$   and $12.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $B$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{B}={4,8,12}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-86590/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a55a708-abb0-5e23-8862-153561d022c8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86590"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-91157/selection/467d029a4c91107a5785f70ee7fcb9a0a328ee99475cd361c0cf843bfe99866a" :answer/id #uuid "a1a7de62-7a35-54d1-8c8d-37d7f5614485" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-91157/selection/9b817f7e57f68a2298ae04ac6999fcdcc0c60c0ee6c6bcb3d669c3e7c7227f90" :answer/id #uuid "998c5e56-9f8c-5bc2-96d7-f5db11fcaabb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-91157/selection/97603d1ee08ecc46bc10a5fb5b84b6750645b92f3d5dc92d550c8f7bb2b97a15" :answer/id #uuid "f504898f-1440-5d44-84d4-545d39402603" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-91157/selection/62179e8135a09160b1013ee76594bcc547affe88edf63462fdf820242489a3d9" :answer/id #uuid "f43e5710-c564-555a-9a7f-521cd35962f5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-91157/selection/fcd8be38da3e727db73089ccb8454f24575d6e10ae3ed5047fe87f8a455824b2" :answer/id #uuid "a1e7a766-c691-56f0-aed9-b86ed86706a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-91157/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "91453757-9831-5a7f-a75f-008cfb4d956e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-91157/selection/62179e8135a09160b1013ee76594bcc547affe88edf63462fdf820242489a3d9" :answer-field/choices ["q-91157/selection/467d029a4c91107a5785f70ee7fcb9a0a328ee99475cd361c0cf843bfe99866a" "q-91157/selection/9b817f7e57f68a2298ae04ac6999fcdcc0c60c0ee6c6bcb3d669c3e7c7227f90" "q-91157/selection/97603d1ee08ecc46bc10a5fb5b84b6750645b92f3d5dc92d550c8f7bb2b97a15" "q-91157/selection/62179e8135a09160b1013ee76594bcc547affe88edf63462fdf820242489a3d9" "q-91157/selection/fcd8be38da3e727db73089ccb8454f24575d6e10ae3ed5047fe87f8a455824b2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-91157" :question/id #uuid "bc8df3f8-8c99-53c4-bedf-bdbc4a64bd8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-91157" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -13 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above ${a}_{33}=-2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -10 & 4 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2 & -6 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -13 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-91157/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "908b96db-9463-50b5-89a3-056072c930ba"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-91157"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186261529 :question/answer-fields 17592186274974] {:db/id "q-73670/selection/ma-v1/77101addf406ee24e5806850f4ba6927a5f743e6512433e364e531c1d0d7f774/9203b5018fbc3a9f5000b15d6d1d272426dc93fe84b540ed66fd69f682e0c56f" :answer/id #uuid "09210f10-b8e1-5b53-b514-bf6ec809e7d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}}{2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73670/selection/ma-v1/77101addf406ee24e5806850f4ba6927a5f743e6512433e364e531c1d0d7f774/0891ccae4b4fc7f7bac24e15877a192dd0bce2c6810ff04dc40be1817f45de6b" :answer/id #uuid "ea046301-b52b-51b5-b5e3-2987d189c450" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73670/selection/ma-v1/77101addf406ee24e5806850f4ba6927a5f743e6512433e364e531c1d0d7f774/6999e6ef207623bb72d27cd697326f02933b332ba460e06790c212c392e4aeb7" :answer/id #uuid "c8f0dfdd-a703-5c27-863a-3f2b430e8dff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73670/selection/ma-v1/77101addf406ee24e5806850f4ba6927a5f743e6512433e364e531c1d0d7f774/74d004bc66bec74e4b76b000523595c4dc4d859eaee6e9c34de9390165c180dc" :answer/id #uuid "d3fd5494-e85a-5ea2-828b-28ffa53b89ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73670/selection/ma-v1/77101addf406ee24e5806850f4ba6927a5f743e6512433e364e531c1d0d7f774/a7bfbad5d25cbf0db0c638a33e20261ed8c1972a6bdfe9a9def8bf982e50b84e" :answer/id #uuid "0ba24c21-ec99-5c40-b60c-04156921d045" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73670/selection/ma-v1/77101addf406ee24e5806850f4ba6927a5f743e6512433e364e531c1d0d7f774" :answer-field/id #uuid "e1e28240-4487-558e-9517-19ef2663b2b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73670/selection/ma-v1/77101addf406ee24e5806850f4ba6927a5f743e6512433e364e531c1d0d7f774/0891ccae4b4fc7f7bac24e15877a192dd0bce2c6810ff04dc40be1817f45de6b" :answer-field/choices ["q-73670/selection/ma-v1/77101addf406ee24e5806850f4ba6927a5f743e6512433e364e531c1d0d7f774/9203b5018fbc3a9f5000b15d6d1d272426dc93fe84b540ed66fd69f682e0c56f" "q-73670/selection/ma-v1/77101addf406ee24e5806850f4ba6927a5f743e6512433e364e531c1d0d7f774/0891ccae4b4fc7f7bac24e15877a192dd0bce2c6810ff04dc40be1817f45de6b" "q-73670/selection/ma-v1/77101addf406ee24e5806850f4ba6927a5f743e6512433e364e531c1d0d7f774/6999e6ef207623bb72d27cd697326f02933b332ba460e06790c212c392e4aeb7" "q-73670/selection/ma-v1/77101addf406ee24e5806850f4ba6927a5f743e6512433e364e531c1d0d7f774/74d004bc66bec74e4b76b000523595c4dc4d859eaee6e9c34de9390165c180dc" "q-73670/selection/ma-v1/77101addf406ee24e5806850f4ba6927a5f743e6512433e364e531c1d0d7f774/a7bfbad5d25cbf0db0c638a33e20261ed8c1972a6bdfe9a9def8bf982e50b84e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-73670"] :question/worked-solution "Let's introduce the new variable $u={2}^{z}-9.$ Differentiating gives \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}z}={2}^{z}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,\\text{d}u={2}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{2}^{z}}{\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}}\\,\\text{d}z & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}}\\cdot {2}^{z}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\cdot \\frac{{u}^{1/2}}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{{2}^{z}-9}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/answer-fields ["q-73670/selection/ma-v1/77101addf406ee24e5806850f4ba6927a5f743e6512433e364e531c1d0d7f774"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-81063/selection/e5f97646ed7e2378ca90a40960516678fe454ec263dda25b3bd55a623a98deb3" :answer/id #uuid "5c4785b1-9940-5c81-bfb9-d993312c70d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5-2(x-1)-6(x-1)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81063/selection/21a375d30df39f9fae06eeaf9df2c6456d2f60fd8fb9f9e1fa720a4bc2e3c09d" :answer/id #uuid "0d5dac73-ec22-5f59-b6b4-5af467826122" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5+2(x-1)+6(x-1)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81063/selection/ff30fa1ef986d59d6a341302e56d655c7774df5b0059925fff17c78fd88c113e" :answer/id #uuid "db86223e-0460-570a-80e8-13ae73d77628" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5-2(x-1)+6(x-1)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81063/selection/80343ce3d7d8e372742a29d23337e627f105ee1e71c26cb8421c8edfadb74883" :answer/id #uuid "51ef6dd2-41b9-5ce9-a150-e2e384cdbc9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5+2(x-1)-6(x-1)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81063/selection/e027906b2b1f8e88bbc23b264c76d41fb801f3daf0494bc038c70e2f9b61744f" :answer/id #uuid "c7b707c4-8e0c-5a96-87b0-7024112b8190" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5-2(x-1)-6(x-1)^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81063/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c95bab29-2e85-5424-9339-70f5b63e00c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81063/selection/ff30fa1ef986d59d6a341302e56d655c7774df5b0059925fff17c78fd88c113e" :answer-field/choices ["q-81063/selection/e5f97646ed7e2378ca90a40960516678fe454ec263dda25b3bd55a623a98deb3" "q-81063/selection/21a375d30df39f9fae06eeaf9df2c6456d2f60fd8fb9f9e1fa720a4bc2e3c09d" "q-81063/selection/ff30fa1ef986d59d6a341302e56d655c7774df5b0059925fff17c78fd88c113e" "q-81063/selection/80343ce3d7d8e372742a29d23337e627f105ee1e71c26cb8421c8edfadb74883" "q-81063/selection/e027906b2b1f8e88bbc23b264c76d41fb801f3daf0494bc038c70e2f9b61744f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81063" :question/id #uuid "9a4ea253-fa70-53c3-a318-c123823ef429" :question/math-academy-id "q-81063" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035241/assets/e483403ebe85920111334dacfc22dc907ab3c33cd38b33361d7634132032c811.png)\n\nThe figure above shows the graph of a function $y=f(x).$ Which of the following could be the second-degree Taylor polynomial for $f$ about $x=1?$" :question/worked-solution "The second-degree Taylor polynomial for $f(x)$ about $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n{P}_{2}(x)=f(1)+{f}^{′}(1)(x-1)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(1)}{2}(x-1)^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the graph, we observe:\n\n- $f(1)<0.$ Therefore, the first term of the Taylor polynomial must be negative.\n\n- ${f}^{′}(1)<0,$ because the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is negative. Therefore, the coefficient of the second term in the Taylor polynomial must be negative.\n\n- ${f}^{″}(1)>0,$ because the graph is concave up at $x=1.$ Therefore, the coefficient of the third term in the Taylor polynomial must be positive.\n\nThe only option that meets the above criteria is\n\n$$\n{P}_{2}(x)=-5-2(x-1)+6(x-1)^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-81063/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fce4cd5a-537a-5eb4-a610-59d2bad95a89"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81063"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181650/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" :answer/id #uuid "8a2cf20a-ca85-5e76-9484-c94bba0c2e0e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181650/selection/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d" :answer/id #uuid "bdfb459d-8b6a-5825-ba85-e93e5558c854" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181650/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" :answer/id #uuid "c6224064-e17b-5a88-8eeb-f8120458eeb4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181650/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" :answer/id #uuid "2e801901-b054-53c2-808f-63df7f57d62b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181650/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c" :answer/id #uuid "595ec850-5ff2-5096-9651-14e2c176c148" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181650/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e6351af-a204-5bd6-a530-20549d869c24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-181650/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" :answer-field/choices ["q-181650/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" "q-181650/selection/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d" "q-181650/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" "q-181650/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" "q-181650/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181650" :question/id #uuid "87fac738-be75-5c4f-b28e-2dae5cd5923b" :question/math-academy-id "q-181650" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are infinite?\n\n- $A={{f}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}}$\n- $B={{g}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}}$\n- $C={{h}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x)\\,:\\,n\\in {N}_{0}}$" :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements.\n\n- The set $A$ is infinite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{(0)}(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\ {f}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\ {f}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x \\\\ {f}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x,8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,…}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $A$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $B$ is finite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{(0)}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {g}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {g}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {g}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {g}^{(4)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $B$ contains four elements:\n\n$$\nB={-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $|B|=4,$ which is finite.\n\n- The set $C$ is infinite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{(0)}(x) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x \\\\ {h}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ {h}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)=2{sec}^{3}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\nC={\\operatorname{sec}⁡x,\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,2{sec}^{3}⁡x-\\operatorname{sec}⁡x,…}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $C$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ and $C$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-181650/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26758016-ed47-562a-9338-85c71ffbeaa9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181650"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181704/field-1/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "91dcc00f-f2c8-5426-abf6-ea1bd962502f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181704/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6dc9ed36-2e28-53d3-b481-63ba06aab151" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-181704/field-1/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-181704/field-1/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181704/field-2/12b48b00f9c1ff14570ca66bc629787a88856efba1cda24cfb28da58c148801a" :answer/id #uuid "c7b45060-96c6-56b3-8a7a-8c9256323089" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181704/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "2197653f-5856-51b3-ae3c-3a6c052c22e4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-181704/field-2/12b48b00f9c1ff14570ca66bc629787a88856efba1cda24cfb28da58c148801a" :answer-field/choices ["q-181704/field-2/12b48b00f9c1ff14570ca66bc629787a88856efba1cda24cfb28da58c148801a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181704/field-3/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "813b7692-a886-5db2-af35-a22870db92f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181704/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "5af16cba-3ced-5c9a-b277-4dd0c6700f60" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-181704/field-3/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer-field/choices ["q-181704/field-3/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181704" :question/id #uuid "926edf84-42b1-556a-b7aa-63fc4baac279" :question/math-academy-id "q-181704" :question/problem "Find the missing coefficients in the conditional definition of the set ${2,3-\\text{i},3+\\text{i}}$ given below.\n\n${2,3-\\text{i},3+\\text{i}}={z\\in C\\,:\\,{z}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n${z}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$z\\,-$\n{{field-3}}\n$=0}$" :question/worked-solution "The given set contains the roots $z\\in C$ of some cubic polynomial $p(z).$\n\nSince the cubic polynomial has roots ${z}_{1}=2,$ ${z}_{2}=3-\\text{i},$ and ${z}_{3}=3+\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(z) & =a(z-{z}_{1})(z-{z}_{2})(z-{z}_{3}) \\\\  & =(1)(z-2)(z-(3-\\text{i}))(z-(3+\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(z-2)({z}^{2}-z(3+\\text{i})-z(3-\\text{i})+(3-\\text{i})(3+\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(z-2)({z}^{2}-6z+10) \\\\  & ={z}^{3}-6{z}^{2}+10z-2{z}^{2}+12z-20 \\\\  & ={z}^{3}-8{z}^{2}+22z-20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as\n\n$$\n{2,3-\\text{i},3+\\text{i}}={z\\in C\\,:\\,{z}^{3}-8{z}^{2}+22z-20=0}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-181704/field-1" "q-181704/field-2" "q-181704/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad21350b-2e3b-57ee-a28c-32a7bd1b2513"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181704"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-19777/selection/9d4fc0fcef5e12c3e623d5852d96cbf00e730c3265727c05d53994c6fdb1d4b9" :answer/id #uuid "f6877b03-36f1-5530-b6f7-2a05f7f903e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9j+2k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19777/selection/066e218fc69849bf48afbe2f33e4f3e83919dfef4dfb2db86ccd97bea480129b" :answer/id #uuid "0b3624ea-5bda-5907-aac1-9ee497758727" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6j-3k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19777/selection/1c2e034d95039750d0dd552d4cac07e20921d0e4811a267a42816876908d5f71" :answer/id #uuid "f18e7b53-2d26-5157-82ee-56b87f8dd998" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9j-6k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19777/selection/0e60c43a1ba30217402c8fb307e87864569125b847d7de9eff8ee6fd839798fd" :answer/id #uuid "ae133177-1618-5d14-b6e2-296ab61003ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6i-2j" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19777/selection/d32360010517a17f4040b83620322e4acda692fca9b883ed7d6db90c955440bf" :answer/id #uuid "5f5ff3f5-9d6a-5c60-ad94-17325fbe13b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9j+6k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19777/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a74272dc-ecf7-5b7f-8a1c-c37d16d42024" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-19777/selection/1c2e034d95039750d0dd552d4cac07e20921d0e4811a267a42816876908d5f71" :answer-field/choices ["q-19777/selection/9d4fc0fcef5e12c3e623d5852d96cbf00e730c3265727c05d53994c6fdb1d4b9" "q-19777/selection/066e218fc69849bf48afbe2f33e4f3e83919dfef4dfb2db86ccd97bea480129b" "q-19777/selection/1c2e034d95039750d0dd552d4cac07e20921d0e4811a267a42816876908d5f71" "q-19777/selection/0e60c43a1ba30217402c8fb307e87864569125b847d7de9eff8ee6fd839798fd" "q-19777/selection/d32360010517a17f4040b83620322e4acda692fca9b883ed7d6db90c955440bf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-19777" :question/id #uuid "67fdf3c0-7b47-568c-a0de-0f280923b37c" :question/math-academy-id "q-19777" :question/problem "Find $(2a+3c)\\times (b+2c)$, if $a\\times b=3i-2j+k$, $a\\times c=j-2k$ and $b\\times c=2i-3j.$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall that:\n\n- The cross product distributes over addition/subtraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a\\pm b)\\times c & =a\\times c\\pm b\\times c \\\\ c\\times (a\\pm b) & =c\\times a\\pm c\\times b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product is associative with respect to scalar multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda a)\\times b & =\\lambda (a\\times b) \\\\ a\\times (\\lambda b) & =\\lambda (a\\times b)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The cross product of parallel vectors equals the zero vector. In particular,\n\n$$\na\\times a=0.\n$$\n\n- The cross product is anticommutative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =-b\\times a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's evaluate our expression:\n\n- First, we use the distributive property:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2a+3c)\\times (b+2c) & = \\\\ ((2a)\\times b)+((2a)\\times (2c))+((3c)\\times b)+((3c)\\times (2c))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we factor out the scalars:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}((2a)\\times b)+((2a)\\times (2c))+((3c)\\times b)+((3c)\\times (2c)) & = \\\\ 2(a\\times b)+(2\\cdot 2)(a\\times c)+3(c\\times b)+(3\\cdot 2)(c\\times c) & = \\\\ 2(a\\times b)+4(a\\times c)+3(c\\times b)+6(c\\times c)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we use anticommutativity, and the fact that $c\\times c=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(a\\times b)+4(a\\times c)+3(c\\times b)+6(c\\times c) & = \\\\ 2(a\\times b)+4(a\\times c)-3(b\\times c)+6(0) & = \\\\ 2(a\\times b)+4(a\\times c)-3(b\\times c)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we substitute the given values and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(a\\times b)+4(a\\times c)-3(b\\times c) & = \\\\ 2(3i-2j+k)+4(j-2k)-3(2i-3j) & = \\\\ (6i-4j+2k)+(4j-8k)-(6i-9j) & = \\\\ (6i-6i)+(-4j+4j+9j)+(2k-8k) & = \\\\ 9j-6k\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-19777/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} 